# ShellCheck configuration for version-management-setup
# https://github.com/koalaman/shellcheck/wiki/Directive

# SC2155: Declare and assign separately to avoid masking return values.
# This project consistently uses `local var=$(cmd)` as a style choice.
# The return-value masking risk is acknowledged and acceptable here.
disable=SC2155

# SC1091: Not following sourced files (dynamic/conditional paths).
disable=SC1091

# SC2034: Variable appears unused. Library modules export functions/vars
# that are consumed by other scripts.
disable=SC2034

# SC2329: Function is never invoked. Library modules define functions
# that are called after sourcing.
disable=SC2329

# SC2015: Note that A && B || C is not if-then-else. Used intentionally
# throughout as a concise pattern for simple conditionals. P2-9 re-justified
# (2026-10-08): 120 occurrences across 115 scripts; each is a
# guard-with-fallback where C is an independent fallback action (log/return),
# not a mutually-exclusive else. Moving to 120 inline suppressions would add
# churn to mutation-critical code for no safety gain; kept global by
# deliberate decision. New code should still prefer explicit if/then/else.
disable=SC2015

# SC2181 (Check exit code directly, not via $?) was moved to INLINE
# suppressions (P2-9, 2026-10-08): its 7 sites in lib/backup.sh, lib/cache.sh
# and version-manager.sh now carry `# shellcheck disable=SC2181` with a reason.
# Removed from the global list so new $?-checks are flagged.

# SC2016: Single-quoted strings intentionally prevent expansion
# (e.g. in help text, templates, log messages).
disable=SC2016

# SC2059: printf with color variables is used throughout.
disable=SC2059

# SC2012: ls is used for human-readable output in diagnostic/display code.
disable=SC2012

# SC2129: Multiple redirects to same file is clearer for separate sections.
disable=SC2129

# (SC2034 was listed twice; the duplicate was removed in P2-9, 2026-10-08.
# The single declaration above covers library export/consumption vars.)
